The library's common work unit and workload are one invoked operation per call, including an absent selection and a refusing call; construction and verifier calls count as their own operations, not as additional entries or numerical work of the parent. The library supplies the spans, full arguments/results and the explicit refusal outcome event, not duplicate counter increments. FIXTURES is registered in the common subscriber's operation-kind dispatch and metric stem roster, using fixtures__root__amend__storage__fixture_replay_interface with the existing common instruments; its fixture_owner_accounting control witnesses its own count and elapsed sample at default and trace without charging another owner. The runtime registration and its witness are distinct from the source census's owner row. From these spans the common subscriber derives started/completed and work-operation counters, the active-operation gauge, inclusive elapsed seconds and workload-operation histograms; no new fixture resource metric or numerical meter is selected. Delegated numerical, encoding, position, replay, read and audit consumption keeps its existing owners and units, unavailable CPU/allocation usage is not zero, and parent durations are not summed with child durations. The library installs no subscriber.

