**Amendment (Released title and marker evidence)** · `amend:decomposition:title-marker-evidence` network-v0.37.0-draft.2 settles party derivation and authorization under ``def:graph:settlement-parties`` and ``itm:graph:settlement-recognition-authorization``. The graph lane’s bite-4 follow-up owns (`verif:design:settlement-party-cases`); bite 5 inherits that title reading for recipients, with its Invitation hold closed and Invitations netting in cells under ``lem:epoch:authored-vouch-withdrawable``. pn-records retains title-certificate fault inputs and pn-verification recomputes the fold in bite 4; pn-epoch checks accepted tentative/final agreement in bite 5; host bite 8 publishes and monitors every boundary, and bite 9 reproduces it offline under (`verif:design:title-certificate-cases`). Records’ bite-2 burn surface distinguishes accumulators and epoch markers; pn-epoch’s bite-5 ledger and bite-7 closure join closed epochs to markers under (`verif:design:marker-registration-cases`). Host and deployment bite 8 own the finality-breach halt and published re-anchor or follow decision under (`verif:design:finality-breach-cases`), with offline bite 9 and integrated bite 11 evidence. These are implementation and deployment obligations, not implemented by the release refresh; package boundaries and bite order remain unchanged.

**Amendment (Public authentication evidence)** · `amend:decomposition:act-authentication` pn-act-authentication owns the public fixed-size carriers, strict qualification and key scripts, signing-key byte hash and initial-asset locator derivation. The pure recipes use the already admitted RustCrypto sha2, tracing and thiserror crates; serde_json is test-only. Canonical authentication encoding adds the planned pn-interchange, pn-records and pn-act-profile edges for the single canonical codec and the existing public act carriers and recipe identifiers. The public verification candidate adds only the pinned secp256k1-zkp re-export edge under (`amend:crypto:public-verification-admission`), with no feature-union change. pn-wallet adds the shared-carrier edge and interprets a decoded transaction with supplied token prevouts. No direct base-library or secret-home edge is added by these pure operations; the later signature and signing surfaces remain under (`dec:design:authentication-owner`) and their operation admission. This is the created public subset of that owner, not admission of its planned private operations. The designed successor separates typed closure messages from courtesy request/receipt messages. Both use the fixed-message verifier with independently selected authority context, but no receipt role is accepted as proposal, seal or approval. No new verifier or duplicate parser is introduced; separate feature/module surfaces must compile alone before implementation admission.

